        <h2 id="b1"><span class="num">1</span>Introduction</h2>
        <h3 id="b1-1"><span class="num">1.1</span>The idea</h3>
        <p>The paper sits on a specific gap in three literatures that rarely meet. Portfolio-construction work picks assets well but rebalances on a fixed calendar and says nothing about timing. Volume–price indicators give timing signals but are decoupled from selection. Deep reinforcement learning adapts, but almost always on a universe someone else fixed. N-EIF is an attempt to put all three in one pipeline where each layer's job is separable — and, crucially, <em>measurable</em> on its own.</p>
        <p>The genuinely new component is the VPI. Conventional indicators such as RSI or MACD read patterns in price. The VPI reads a pattern one level up: it asks whether the <em>relationship</em> between volume and price is currently stable or unstable. The motivation is an old observation in market microstructure that linear volume–price models leave autocorrelated residuals — evidence of misspecification. Rather than treat that as a nuisance, the paper turns it into the signal.</p>
        <h3 id="b1-2"><span class="num">1.2</span>The hypothesis</h3>
        <p>The framework is a stack of three layers, so the claim is stated as a hierarchy, and each step is falsifiable on its own:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>GA selection beats the index.</b> A genetic-algorithm basket, held passively, should outperform simply holding the KOSPI 200.</li>
          <li><b>VPI gating beats the GA basket held passively.</b> Adding rule-based VPI timing on the same basket should add return.</li>
          <li><b>The learned agent adds something on top of the rule.</b> Replacing the pure rule with the VPI-and-DQN consensus should add further — and if it does not, the reinforcement-learning layer is decoration.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>There is a fourth, implicit claim which turns out to be the most interesting one: that the DQN is not independently useful. The paper tests standalone LSTM-DQN as its own strategy specifically so that this can be seen.</p>

